00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.610
as if you just chugged it
all in one or two sittings?

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.630
It's not the same.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.760
Your body can only absorb so much water

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.530
and if it doesn't absorb it,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.739
it then goes to waste
and you create urine.

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:43.980
(whooshing)
Which is more important,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.330
inhaling or exhaling?

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:46.590
Okay. This is important.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:47.970
Inhaling.
(chuckles)

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.610
Inhaling or ex-
(heaving breathing)

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.860
Honestly, as important it is to inhale.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.320
I think the exhale is the underrated

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.140
because you can really
get a lot from an exhale.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.730
I don't wanna go too spiritual with it

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.930
but it cleanses the soul.
(twinkle sounding)

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.100
And essentially when you're inhaling,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:02.933
you're getting oxygen.

00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:04.170
Yeah. Okay. Good stuff.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.125
But when you're exhaling.

00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:05.958
(exhaling)

00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:06.873
Carbon dioxide.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.580
Co2.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.320
C-O-O-L.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.249
Cool
