00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.030
That's actually a classic thing

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.490
and I talked about it with
Matthew Walker on my podcast.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.650
Where if you're making up sleep debt,

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:20.550
where you haven't slept

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.020
for a certain number of nights in a row,

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.130
the adequate numbers of sleep,

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.050
and then you finally get
a good night's sleep.

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:27.510
That initial few minutes of waking up,

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:29.670
you're gonna feel terrible
because of sleep inertia.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.580
Where you haven't yet kind
of cleared that sleep debt

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.680
and you probably need to
sleep a few more nights

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.157
in order to start feeling better.

00:08:36.157 --> 00:08:38.160
"I heard if you're having
breakouts on your forehead

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.570
it's because of bad gut health.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.640
Is this true and how can
I improve my gut health?"

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.800
Okay, I'm gonna take the second
part of the question first.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.090
You can improve your gut health

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.170
by focusing on the things

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.730
we talk about quite often in this channel.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.110
Eating fibrous foods,

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.790
those are basically prebiotics.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:53.070
Eating a wide variety of plants,

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.630
AKA fruits and vegetables.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.210
Limiting the amount of
simple sugars you consume

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.790
because those things can
actually worsen gut health.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.580
Now let's talk about acne on the forehead.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.100
Maybe if you're eating
a really unhealthy diet,

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.080
also having a really unhealthy lifestyle,

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.460
and not sleeping in all these things,

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.710
yeah you might get a breakout
because of a hormonal issue.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:13.110
But it changing just one little aspect

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.050
is not gonna have a drastic
outcome on your skin.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.510
You need to think about all
the variables in your life

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.280
and try and improve your lifestyle

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.960
as opposed to finding a hack here.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:22.987
That's not the secret.

00:09:22.987 --> 00:09:24.870
"What's the difference
between a first, second,

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:25.860
and third degree burn?"

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.693
Depth.

00:09:26.693 --> 00:09:27.526
Depth.

00:09:27.526 --> 00:09:28.740
(typing)

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:29.760
First degree burns

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.680
only affect the outer layer of the skin.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.610
Second degree burns

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.830
affect outer and underlying layer of skin.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:35.910
And third degree burns

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:37.530
affect the deep layers of the skin.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:38.670
See, I even had to look that up

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:41.689
even though the answer was
outer, outer and inner, or deep.

00:09:41.689 --> 00:09:43.230
(chuckles)

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.670
But see, this is stuff at med school

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.770
that you shouldn't spend hours memorizing

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.670
'cause what ends up happening

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.200
is you learn a lot of useless information

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.160
that you could look up real quick.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.330
And that's what the new generation

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.980
of medical student and doctor should be.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.300
Someone that knows a lot,

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:55.710
but knows things that they can forget

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:56.730
that they can look up real quick.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:57.810
'Cause the ease of information

00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.160
is right there at our fingertips.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:09:59.993
So for example,

00:09:59.993 --> 00:10:01.170
guidelines change all the time

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.250
when it comes to screenings.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.570
I try not to memorize those

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:05.370
because I know that at any
moment I can look it up

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.660
and get the most up-to-date info.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:07.770
Even if I know it cold,

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:09.330
I still look it up cause I want to be sure

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.046
that I'm giving you the
best healthcare advice.

